WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.851
DNA is a very long molecule. It is made of many small repeating units, joined in a chain. Each unit is called a nucleotide. RNA, a single-stranded molecule that helps make proteins, is made of nucleotides too.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:31.149
Each nucleotide carries one base. A base is a small part that works like a letter of a code. DNA has four bases: adenine, thymine, cytosine and guanine. We write them as A, T, C and G.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:45.071
Now look at one nucleotide. It has three parts. Find the sugar first. It is the five-sided shape in the middle, joined to both other parts. In DNA, the sugar is called deoxyribose.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:56.253
On the outer side of the sugar is the phosphate group. It is often drawn as a small circle. On the other side is the base. So the order is phosphate, sugar, base.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:08.477
In a DNA molecule, sugar and phosphate join in turn to make a long backbone. The bases point inwards, like the rungs of a ladder. A rung is one step of the ladder.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:18.458
Spell the names with care. In DNA the sugar is deoxyribose. Ribose is the sugar in RNA. And write phosphate, not phosphorus.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:29.162
If a question says describe, do not just list the parts. Say what is joined to what. The phosphate is joined to the sugar. The base is joined to the sugar too.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:42.865
Here is a real exam question. DNA is formed from nucleotides. The diagram shows a single nucleotide. Name the parts labelled R, S and T. It is worth three marks.

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:52.879
Start with S. It is the five-sided shape in the middle, joined to both other parts. So S is the sugar. In DNA, it is deoxyribose.

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:58.357
R is the small circle on the outer side of the sugar. So R is the phosphate.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:09.169
T is on the other side of the sugar. In DNA it would pair with a base on the other strand. So T is a base. You could also name one, such as adenine.

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:16.257
Here is the full answer. This answer is written by olevels.com. It is not the official mark scheme.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:27.896
A common mistake is to call the repeating unit an amino acid, or a gene. Amino acids build proteins. The unit of DNA is a nucleotide.

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:37.879
Another mistake is to say the bases make the backbone. They do not. The backbone is only sugar and phosphate. The bases are the rungs in the middle.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:03:01.093
Your turn. This nucleotide comes from RNA, not DNA. Part J is a small circle on the outside. Part K is the five-sided shape in the middle. Part L is a rectangle on the other side. Name J, K and L. Then say which part is different from a DNA nucleotide. Pause here and work it out.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:13.059
Part a. Use the positions. J, the circle on the outside, is the phosphate. K, in the middle, is the sugar. This is RNA, so it is ribose. L is the base.

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:21.287
Part b. The sugar is different. A DNA nucleotide has deoxyribose. An RNA nucleotide has ribose.

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:33.178
So, every time: find the sugar in the middle first. The phosphate is on the outer side. The base is on the other side. Use the exact names: phosphate and deoxyribose.
